01:05:36.965 --> 01:05:43.540
So, that stretch of the where the confluence of the Hop River and the Skunkamug River

01:05:43.700 --> 01:05:44.420
is

01:05:44.580 --> 01:05:48.820
pretty significant habitat for wood turtles, which are a state listed species.

01:05:49.860 --> 01:05:50.500
The

01:05:50.980 --> 01:05:55.455
primary use of the site is the floodplain habitat that is

01:05:55.935 --> 01:05:59.695
along the Skokamug River and that especially that open area

01:06:00.575 --> 01:06:03.855
on the property that is along the Hop River.

01:06:04.495 --> 01:06:06.575
Both of those are heavily used by wood turtles.

01:06:07.990 --> 01:06:10.230
I took looking at the project,

01:06:11.670 --> 01:06:12.950
the location

01:06:13.350 --> 01:06:16.150
of where the proposed residences and

01:06:16.470 --> 01:06:27.525
the activities associated with the development there, I don't anticipate any real direct impacts on any wood turtle habitat because everything is pretty much outside of the floodplain.

01:06:28.485 --> 01:06:30.565
There would be my main concern

01:06:30.725 --> 01:06:32.085
would be during

01:06:32.085 --> 01:06:34.805
any construction activities or development activities

01:06:36.170 --> 01:06:39.450
for the residents and for the site would be to prevent

01:06:39.610 --> 01:06:43.850
any turtles from moving into the site and potentially being harmed.

01:06:44.090 --> 01:06:46.010
And that can be accomplished by some

01:06:47.465 --> 01:06:50.265
exclusionary fencing like sediment control fencing

01:06:50.425 --> 01:06:54.105
to keep them out of areas where heavy machinery is going to be used.

01:06:54.905 --> 01:06:57.305
So the actual development footprint

01:06:57.465 --> 01:07:00.345
is really not so much an issue. It's

01:07:00.345 --> 01:07:02.825
pretty easy to handle excluding the turtles.

01:07:03.840 --> 01:07:06.800
My primary concern is one more associated

01:07:06.800 --> 01:07:07.360
with

01:07:08.160 --> 01:07:08.880
the

01:07:08.960 --> 01:07:10.560
use of the property

01:07:11.680 --> 01:07:12.960
along the

01:07:13.680 --> 01:07:15.360
Hop River there on the Skunkamug.

01:07:18.055 --> 01:07:19.095
There's

01:07:19.095 --> 01:07:22.295
been some clearings there and there's been some gardens. And those are

01:07:22.535 --> 01:07:24.935
and there's a footpath that goes through there.

01:07:25.095 --> 01:07:26.855
And those activities,

01:07:27.975 --> 01:07:30.535
while not necessarily

01:07:33.950 --> 01:07:40.910
too impactful for wood turtles, they can be. They can have a significant impact if best management practices aren't followed.

01:07:41.150 --> 01:07:43.230
So if you look at the recommendations

01:07:43.230 --> 01:07:44.110
that I proposed,

01:07:44.935 --> 01:07:51.255
a fair amount of them are focused on looking at what activities occur within those areas

01:07:51.495 --> 01:07:54.055
and when they occur and how they occur.

01:07:54.375 --> 01:07:57.575
Anything outside of the dormant season is best

01:07:58.180 --> 01:08:01.220
for the turtles because that prevents any

01:08:01.540 --> 01:08:03.140
potential impacts to them.

01:08:03.540 --> 01:08:06.420
And the impact is really one that is less

01:08:06.660 --> 01:08:09.460
on the habitat and more on trying to prevent

01:08:09.620 --> 01:08:10.980
mortality of turtles

01:08:11.575 --> 01:08:14.935
that may be moving into that area and utilizing that area,

01:08:15.335 --> 01:08:18.455
because it's used pretty heavily for basking by the turtles,

01:08:18.615 --> 01:08:20.295
some nesting by the turtles,

01:08:20.695 --> 01:08:23.095
and there's even some hibernation occurring in the

01:08:24.760 --> 01:08:28.040
concentration of them there and a stretch of the river right on that side.

01:08:28.520 --> 01:08:31.480
So in sum, there really are two considerations.

01:08:31.480 --> 01:08:37.080
One are those that are excluding turtles from when there's construction activity associated

01:08:37.080 --> 01:08:38.675
with the proposed

01:08:39.235 --> 01:08:40.035
development.

01:08:40.115 --> 01:08:41.714
And then the second is

01:08:41.875 --> 01:08:48.675
ongoing activities that might occur within that floodplain area or the upland area adjacent to the floodplain

01:08:48.675 --> 01:08:50.035
during the active season.

01:08:50.660 --> 01:08:55.540
So I provide various levels of recommendations depending on what planned activities

01:08:55.620 --> 01:08:56.740
